(5426408, 778267, 104020, '<td valign="top">Thnakyou for voting on my first picture.  I was expecting to get around 5 which is pretty much what i got, however i did get some 10''s which surprised me, as it is not that good.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-04-13 12:14:20.</i></td>', 'Thnakyou for voting on my first picture.  I was expecting to get around 5 which is pretty much what i got, however i did get some 10''s which surprised me, as it is not that good.', '2009-04-08 11:10:18.000000', '2009-04-13 13:14:20.000000', 0),
(5426595, 777863, 39427, '<td valign="top">congrats on your first ribbon Trevor!  I gave this a 9 and was positive it would place, awesome work.</td>', 'congrats on your first ribbon Trevor!  I gave this a 9 and was positive it would place, awesome work.', '2009-04-08 12:05:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5426598, 778001, 60698, '<td valign="top">Hey we finished near each other on the same page! :) This is so artsy and fabulous! Should have been a higher scorer IMHO, but the voters at here DPC are favoring only certain types of photos these day. A very narrow field of success! I am thinking a photo like this would do well at jpg mag or even....onexposure. Hehe! :)</td>', 'Hey we finished near each other on the same page! :) This is so artsy and fabulous! Should have been a higher scorer IMHO, but the voters at here DPC are favoring only certain types of photos these day. A very narrow field of success! I am thinking a photo like this would do well at jpg mag or even....onexposure. Hehe! :)', '2009-04-08 12:06:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5426674, 777863, 39427, '<td valign="top">btw, I know you got a 6.79 but this shot def should have scored higher... first off it is a wild hawk, which places this image in a different category of fauna pictures, one that i think is much more worthwhile of admiration.  2nd, you don''t see shots like this with the feathers all ruffled and the water splashing, a real original shot with perfect technicals, congrats again.<br/></td>', 'btw, I know you got a 6.79 but this shot def should have scored higher... first off it is a wild hawk, which places this image in a different category of fauna pictures, one that i think is much more worthwhile of admiration.  2nd, you don''t see shots like this with the feathers all ruffled and the water splashing, a real original shot with perfect technicals, congrats again.', '2009-04-08 12:27:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(5426836, 777863, 11793, '<td valign="top">perseverance paid off - quite a capture you have - congrats !<br/> <br/></td>', 'perseverance paid off - quite a capture you have - congrats ! ', '2009-04-08 13:08:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5426892, 777863, 81530, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first ribbon. Hopefully many more to come!</td>', 'Congrats on your first ribbon. Hopefully many more to come!', '2009-04-08 13:33:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5426949, 778273, 68504, '<td valign="top">I sort of knew they weren''t yours, although in a way you have laid claim to a great many Athenian dogs.  What I didn''t suspect was that they really were strays. Handsome, almost plump and placid, they seem just to be lounging in someone''s courtyard - an interesting almost Japanese style one, with the illusion of a small pool in that gren copper plate?  Do people feed them, or do they maintain themselves entirely?  Do they travel and/or just congregate in packs?  What is the general public attitude towards them?</td>', 'I sort of knew they weren''t yours, although in a way you have laid claim to a great many Athenian dogs.  What I didn''t suspect was that they really were strays. Handsome, almost plump and placid, they seem just to be lounging in someone''s courtyard - an interesting almost Japanese style one, with the illusion of a small pool in that gren copper plate?  Do people feed them, or do they maintain themselves entirely?  Do they travel and/or just congregate in packs?  What is the general public attitude towards them?', '2009-04-08 13:54:37.000000', NULL, 0),
